 17592186048483 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192908 #edb/ref 1050 420.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192908 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "53f8a96f-9300-5270-99f9-06fc6fa03819" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193602 #edb/ref 1061 40724 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193602 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "6f436efa-7ff9-5c0c-b1b4-46029ab6b788" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193602 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186192746 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193604 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186193635 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193604 #edb/ref 1061 40957 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193604 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "00cc323b-1079-57c2-bd10-8b8280d6b6cd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193604 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186193860 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193605 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186193602 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193605 #edb/ref 1061 40958 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193605 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "1ec4a8ba-4e50-585a-8d91-2b697329ceeb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193605 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186192748 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193635 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186193605 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193635 #edb/ref 1061 41512 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193635 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "8a4ad5e8-f1f8-5216-8929-a54e602ffd9d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193635 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186192768 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193860 #edb/ref 1064 "We can always represent the solution of an inequality using a number line.\n\nFor example, let's express the solution of the following inequality using a number line:\n\n$$\n5x \\geq 30\n$$\n\nThe variable $x$ is being *multiplied* by $5.$ To isolate $x,$ we can perform the *opposite* operation, which is *dividing* by $5.$ So, we divide both sides of the inequality by $5{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x & \\ge 30 \\\\ \\frac{5x}{5} & \\ge \\frac{30}{5} \\\\ \\frac{5x}{5} & \\ge 6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can cancel a common factor of $5$ from the numerator and denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5x}{5} & \\ge 6 \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{5}x}{\\cancel{5}} & \\ge 6 \\\\ x & \\ge 6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x \\geq 6.$ This solution can be expressed on a number line, as shown below.\n\n![](images/c3/c3a3d5a89d9181af5de9658ad2ac00cd8026a3050d48765dba5f5b23d3a0e7bc.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193860 #edb/ref 1065 6759 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193860 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "c86ff43d-11e0-54fc-bafd-5638148ec372" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193860 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
